WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:17.949 --> 00:00:20.449
So Fox news has been a topic of discussion
lately.

00:00:20.449 --> 00:00:26.440
Are they with Trump fully or are they with
Trump partially or might they abandon Trump

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:32.349
in the 2020 election during yesterday's impeachment
inquiry hearings, Fox news was fully, fully,

00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:38.080
fully, fully with Donald Trump, including
not only their coverage after the fact defending

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:42.660
Donald Trump, but I want to look at some of
the onscreen graphics that they aired during

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:43.660
the hearings.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:47.809
So you might remember that, uh, over the last
couple of years there have been networks who

00:00:47.809 --> 00:00:51.720
have chosen to do something that I think is
really important when Donald Trump is giving

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.909
a speech and telling lie after lie after lie.

00:00:54.909 --> 00:00:57.530
They try to FactCheck Trump in real time.

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:03.339
So Trump is speaking and there will be graphics
on screen that present facts about the things

00:01:03.339 --> 00:01:05.320
Donald Trump is lying about it.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:09.220
They don't do it all the time, but it's been
tested by some networks.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:13.880
When Donald Trump is speaking, Trump tells
a lie and the truth shows up on the screen

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.500
and it's a pretty useful thing.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.090
Fox did a version of this but it's Fox.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:21.060
So they actually did the opposite during yesterday's
hearings.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:27.170
They put up lies and unsubstantiated allegations
about the witnesses on screen or the people

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:30.090
asking questions on screen as if they were
fact.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:36.439
They took, uh, attacks from Donald Trump on
the witnesses and on the members of Congress

00:01:36.439 --> 00:01:41.679
asking questions and put them on screen as
if they were facts that you should be aware

00:01:41.679 --> 00:01:44.689
of in order to understand what was happening
during the hearings.

00:01:44.689 --> 00:01:45.990
So let's look at some examples.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:50.609
This first one is when Adam Schiff was speaking,
and it's really important to do this so that

00:01:50.609 --> 00:01:52.799
you understand the way the propaganda cycle
works.

00:01:52.799 --> 00:01:57.670
And it's also really important because one
of the main criticisms from Republicans of

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:03.200
the witnesses was they are presenting hearsay
and they are just saying what they heard from

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.640
someone else.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:10.970
What Fox news was putting up on screen were
unproven allegations and claims, which during

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:16.510
the hearings Republicans said we shouldn't
actually be doing, we shouldn't be basing

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:19.840
our opinion on things that are unproven claims.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.650
And then Fox puts up unproven claims and assertions.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:29.659
So first of all, Fox news puts up as a fact
that quote Adam Schiff publicly exaggerated

00:02:29.659 --> 00:02:36.150
the substance of the Trump's Olenski phone
call on nine 26 September 26th shifts said

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:42.099
that the transcript of the Trump phone call
reads like a classic organized crime shakedown.

00:02:42.099 --> 00:02:44.819
Now this was shifts interpretation.

00:02:44.819 --> 00:02:46.250
It was made sort of satirically.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:48.719
I mean, you know, it's hyperbolic language.

00:02:48.719 --> 00:02:50.960
It's like an organized crime shape.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:54.459
Shakedown shift said he's not literally saying
that.

00:02:54.459 --> 00:02:59.950
He said, you know, in some and character,
this was what the president was trying to

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:00.950
communicate.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:05.549
And of course it was that phone call was part
of a bigger picture.

00:03:05.549 --> 00:03:08.660
Attempted shakedown of president Zelenskyi
of Ukraine.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:14.670
And in reality shifts summary, even partially
satirical, using hyperbolic language was far

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:19.930
more accurate than the way Donald Trump and
his defenders have summarized that phone call.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:23.519
Fox news, putting that onscreen as it's a
fat as if it's the fact.

00:03:23.519 --> 00:03:30.159
Also on screen at the time, Fox puts on screen
that quote, Schiff admitted to not being clear

00:03:30.159 --> 00:03:32.519
about contact with the whistle blower.

00:03:32.519 --> 00:03:37.109
We still have no evidence that Adam Schiff
was in contact with a whistle blower.

00:03:37.109 --> 00:03:41.829
There is no evidence that shift helped a shift,
helped write the whistleblower complaint as

00:03:41.829 --> 00:03:43.069
has been alleged.

00:03:43.069 --> 00:03:47.810
The white, uh, the whistleblower did go to
a house intelligence committee aid who said,

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:52.390
listen, you need to get a lawyer and you need
to file a formal complaint.

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:55.330
And that aid told Adam Schiff about that.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:59.370
Again, a totally distorted claim on screen.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:00.799
Let's go to the next one.

00:04:00.799 --> 00:04:06.459
This next one gets absolutely ridiculous and
understand that for the Fox news audience,

00:04:06.459 --> 00:04:07.989
this becomes gospel.

00:04:07.989 --> 00:04:11.519
This becomes the truth about the impeachment
hearings.

00:04:11.519 --> 00:04:18.190
Fox put up a graphic that says Trump has repeatedly
implied that shift committed treason.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:24.310
Now, that is absolutely true in the sense
that Trump has implied that, but why is that?

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:25.390
On the screen?

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:31.190
You could put actual facts about the circumstances
on the screen, but instead they put up an

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:36.260
unfounded ad hominem attack from the president
on a member of Congress.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:39.660
Treason is defined very clearly in the constitution.

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:42.280
Schiff clearly did not do anything treasonous.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:43.630
Why would you put that on the screen?

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:46.710
Well, to poison the well, of course.

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:52.250
Then we get to the graphics for former Ukraine
ambassador William Taylor, which there may

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:53.650
be even worse.

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:59.770
Fox puts on screen next to Taylor's face that
quote, president Trump dismissed Taylor as

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:00.770
a never Trumper.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:06.410
Now, once again, it is true that Trump said
that, but that's not something any serious

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.830
news outlet puts on screen during a hearing.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:12.930
If the goal is to better the understanding
of the audience about the substance of what's

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:17.640
being alleged, especially when there is no
evidence that Taylor is a so-called never

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:19.030
Trump or period.

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:20.560
There's really nothing else to debunk.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:22.750
Other than that, I mean there's no evidence.

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:24.280
It's not relevant to the hearings.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:29.840
Fox news decided that the most important things
to tell their audience about shifts and Taylor

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:33.430
are unsubstantiated attacks made by president
Trump.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.030
They're doing Trump's dirty work.

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:36.770
That's ultimately what this comes down to.

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:42.260
So when you watch the hearings, you might
might've been annoyed as I sort of was that

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:47.510
so much time was spent by Democrats clarifying
the reputations and the credentials of the

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:50.850
witnesses and the witnesses talking about,
you know, George kept talking about he's,

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:56.380
I think he said the fourth George Kent, uh,
or Kent from his family to be serving the

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:57.800
government or whatever.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:59.730
Many of us deemed it unnecessary.

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:04.940
We wanted to get to the substance, but this
is part of why it had to be done because in

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:09.650
real time, Republicans bolstered with the
support of right wing media and Republicans,

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:15.210
uh, uh, Republicans and right wing media together
were attempting to smear Adam Schiff.

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:18.040
They were attempting to Smeal smear William
Taylor.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:22.820
They were attempting to smear George Kent
and it was happening on screen in real time

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:23.820
on Fox news.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:29.620
So listen, we don't know ultimately what role
Fox news will choose to play in Donald Trump's

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:33.950
reelection campaign for 2020, as we said,
very different circumstances than under George

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.010
W. Bush in 2004.

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:40.100
We don't know if there'll be fully, partially
or not at all with Trump for his reelection,

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:44.620
but at least as far as the impeachment inquiry
hearings go, they have been Trump's dirty

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:50.320
work henchmen, the equivalent of whoever went
up to stormy Daniels in that garage and implicitly

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:53.240
threatened Stormy's daughter, I believe it
was.

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:54.370
They were doing that work.

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:56.210
Fox news was during the hearings.

